// A provider declares a method whose output is a provider enum, and the rule calls the provider
// without the method, so lowering does not add the enum to the schema. The bridge leaves out the
// method alone: leaving out the whole declaration would make the specification find the invocation
// undeclared. Both accept the set, and allow alice's `Read`.
@id("read_scanned")
permit (principal, action == Drupe::Action::"Read", resource)
when { Risk::Scan(context.input.user) };
